WEBVTT

NOTE LUMO, The Gospel of Luke 12:1-59 (Arclight 6_GOLuke2613), en.
NOTE Timings: whisper.cpp small -dtw small per speech burst on the isolated dialogue (dialoguenhance centre channel), first word on the burst start, 2026-11-06.

1
00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.850
Then Jesus said to his disciples:

2
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.700
Therefore I tell you, do not worry about your life, what you will eat;

3
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.450
or about your body, what you will wear.

4
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.750
For life is more than food, and the body more than clothes.

5
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.900
Consider the ravens: They do not sow or reap,

6
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.900
they have no storeroom or barn; yet God feeds them.

7
00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.200
And how much more valuable you are than birds!

8
00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.100
Who of you by worrying can add a single hour to your life?

9
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.750
Since you cannot do this very little thing,

10
00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.800
why do you worry about the rest?

11
00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:11.900
Consider how the wild flowers grow. They do not labor or spin.

12
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.830
Yet I tell you, not even Solomon in all his splendor

13
00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.600
was dressed like one of these.

14
00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.550
If that is how God clothes the grass of the field,

15
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.800
which is here today, and tomorrow is thrown into the fire,

16
00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:31.150
how much more will he clothe you, you of little faith!

17
00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.600
And do not set your heart on what you will eat or drink;

18
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.100
do not worry about it.

19
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.850
For the pagan world runs after all such things,

20
00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.350
and your Father knows that you need them.

21
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.550
But seek his kingdom, and these things will be given to you as well.

22
00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:56.050
Do not be afraid, little flock,

23
00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.550
for your Father has been pleased to give you the kingdom.

24
00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.100
Sell your possessions and give to the poor.

25
00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.850
Provide purses for yourselves that will not wear out,

26
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.300
a treasure in heaven that will never fail,

27
00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.850
where no thief comes near and no moth destroys.

28
00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.950
For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also.
